ng a government shutdown  but local texas reporters were really  instrumental in reporting the story out  um and you have to i think put into  context that these newsrooms were  reporting last week during a devastating  winter storm and power outage  that rocked the state and so they're  working under these really tough  conditions  and you still had a throng of local  reporters  uh that were you know engaging the  time-tested tradition of  showing up at a politician's doorstep to  confront them on their screw-up  um that video that we just showed you  know was an  abc 13 uh reporter grilling ted cruz  about  the decision to leave to cancun while  his state was dealing with this crisis  um but there was also this great uh  interview that ted cruz got  with a gaggle of reporters where they  were grilling him outside of his home in  texas  about the decision to flee the state and  i think in an era when  you know you have so much hyper partisan  siloed media where ted cruz can just  appear on fox news for an interview with  sean hannity and not get questioned  about this stuff  it's always heartwarming as someone that  covers the media to know that a  politician will still face  tough questions on their doorstep from  local reporters  indeed and now this week's losers greg  kelly at newsmax  who had the courage to go after not the  president of the united states  but to go after his dogs millie  had like a staff and they really took  care of her very beautiful dog  this dog looks like from i'm sorry from  the junkyard and i love that dog  but he looks like he's not been well  cared for no not not at all  thank you for having us uh no he looks  very dirty and disheveled and uh  very unlike a presidential dog so aidan  what do you make of that an attack on  the  first dogs well so  greg kelly uh believe it or not is the  star  anchor of newsmax uh he's the primetime  host over there  uh and newsmax is of course a uh  pro-trump uh conservative tv outlet that  has been challenging fox news in recent  months  um you know i think the segment in which  kelly attacked  joe biden's dog as dirty and even  brought on two historians  to join him in a pretty absurd segment  about it  is good evidence that the network is not  really ready for prime time and then  when it has a bunch of  eyes on it watching it um you you really  realize that it has segments like that  which come off as sort of amateurish  and a little insane um so yeah i think  it's worth remembering that this is a  this is a prime time show  on a news network um let's not get that  lost uh that is actually challenging fox  news right now  and they're struggling to stay ahead  they had some momentum after the  election but they seemed to have lost  that a bit  they have lost that a bit you know right  after the election when trump supporters  which is a really huge and engaged  audience  uh were jumping ship from fox news and  going to newsmax  mainly because fox news despite all of  its support for the president  was not engaging in the fantasy that  trump had actually won the election  until it was stolen from him  newsmax was they were holding out hope  particularly hosts like greg kelly  and he saw his ratings surge because he  was selling that lie to viewers  um that has ceded from the view now that  joe biden is obviously president  and their ratings have gone down in the  aftermath  so he yeah so now they're gonna go after  the dogs we don't know who's next aiden  thanks so much for being here today  thanks to all of you for watching and  thanks to the staff at long crime for  getting us on the air  and off the air  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  you
 

